## Highlights
- Even when my five year old is playing outside, touching grass without a screen in sight, he lives in his imagination. I see a yard where he sees a magical kingdom. We don’t need tech to live in virtual reality. It’s in all of our nature to tell stories and believe them. We naturally build conceptual models and live inside them. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01j2hmth29cqpy7ae3n5rvez8v))
- As parents and teachers, we have no choice but to slowly titrate controlled access and teach our kids to use it better. Kids learn from their mistakes. So with tech, just like with most other areas of life we need to leave room for them to make mistakes in the first place. That’s why I’m more interested in wise education and mental training than I am in outright bans, even if they are necessary in the short term. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01j2hn11rpgy3qfa3c5tgv2vx2))
